[[ ## reasoning ## ]]
The claim states two distinct facts: (1) Khady Sylla was an African writer, and (2) the director of the 1932 American Pre-Code drama film *Afraid to Talk* was not an African writer. The provided summary confirms both facts: Khady Sylla was indeed a Senegalese (African) writer, and Edward L. Cahn, the director of *Afraid to Talk*, was not an African writer. The reasoning involves verifying the accuracy of these two separate claims by cross-referencing the information provided in the summary.

[[ ## query ## ]]
SELECT ?filmDirector WHERE {
  ?filmDirector wikidata:P31 wikidata:Q11424 ;
                wikidata:P57 ?film ;
                rdfs:label ?directorName .
  FILTER(LANG(?directorName) = "en")
  ?film wikidata:P31 wikidata:Q11424 ;
        rdfs:label "Afraid to Talk"@en .
}

